  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cash and Livelihoods Support_CAMKID</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Community Association for Knowledge In Development (CAMKID) is a local organisation providing services and supporting the rights of own-account workers in ethnic minority areas in Northern Laos. They work with labourers, especially women, who are affected by chemicals in banana plantations and with small-scale farmers/informal workers impacted from COVID. They will collaborate with the PTU and local government offices in Bokeo to implement this programme. CAMKID was also involved in the pilot phase. They will support the implementation of Outcomes 1 and 2 in Bokeo and will influence the Provincial People&#x2019;s Assembly (PPA) of Bokeo province and national authorities for the protection of workers&#x2019; rights, focusing on healthcare, OSH, wage, income security, as well as child protection. They will also lobby private companies to ensure better social protection and decent work based on the implementation of existing legal frameworks.

The two associations have decided to collaborate on developing common objectives, in particular those that support a world based on relationships of solidarity and greater justice. The two associations agree that respect for Human Rights, including the Rights of Women and Children, forms part of their commitment, as well as respect for Social and Economic Rights for everyone. The Action that is subject to the present agreement is a contribution towards these objectives but it cannot be considered as the sole link that unites the three associations.

The partner  CAMKID  andOxfam-in-Laos undertake to build a relationship that reinforces each party&#x2019;s work and skills, while developing each organisation&#x2019;s respective strategies.

By way of an example, CAMKID  is interested in taking part in activities that heighten awareness among the Laos public, by sending personnel and/or equipment in relation to the issue concerned by the Action. CAMKID  would also like to take part in the discussions held by the Oxfam-in-Laos on strategic reflections connected with the action.

Oxfam undertakes to share information that may be useful for the missions of CAMKID  andto assist CAMKID  using methodological tools and supports.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAMKID is a local NGO providing services and supporting the rights of own-account workers in ethnic minority areas in Northern Laoswhere many, especially women, are affected by the use of chemicals in banana plantations. CAMKID will contribute to all results in this programme by organising 20 local groups of vegetable and livestock farmers, workers in banana plantations and food processing firms in Northern Laos (Bokeo), totalling 1000 workers, 60% women. CAMKID will strengthen the capacity of workers in the banana plantations, by organizing workers&#x2019; groups. They will collaborate with the LFTU to influence local (especially the Provincial People&#x2019;s Assembly of Bokeo province) and national authorities, for a better implementation of workers&#x2019; rights and the protection of their interests, focusing on healthcare, OSH, wage, income security, as well as child protection. They will influence private companies to ensure better social protection and decent work based on the implementation of existing legal frameworks.

CAMKID respond to Implementing project activity in Bokeo province, monitoring the result indicators, Financial and narrative reporting to Oxfam-in-Laos, Organising joint activity undertaken between partners in target project areas; Participating with other partners and stakeholders in assessment, donor visits, seminars evaluating the progress made towards the Objective; Regular communicating with Oxfam-in-Laos and other another stakeholder about the project implementation; Reporting the project result to Oxfam in Laos as schedule</narrative>
